# Plan: customer satisfaction rating

Spec: `docs/specs/csat-rating.md` (approved, Mai Do, 2026-01-12). Written 2026-10-07. Status: **not started, awaiting owner review of Q1-Q8**.
Stack: plain Node 20, no dependencies. Guardrail: `node --test` (baseline 7/7 pass on `main` at 9b6e07b; `npm` is not on this PATH, `node --test` is what `package.json` runs).
Execution: inline, one commit per phase, checkpoint after each phase (recommended; subagent-driven also works, see `bk-build/references/executing.md`).

## Goal
A customer rates a resolved ticket 1-5 once; a low score emails the assigned agent; a nightly job writes a weekly per-agent summary; `assignee_id` becomes `owner_id`.

## Scope call
Requirement 6 (the rename) is independent of 1-5 and is the only part that touches an outside contract (finance reads `exports/tickets.json`) and the production schema. It is its own phase, last, and can ship later without holding back the rating. Phases 1-3 use `assignee_id`; phase 4 renames everything, new code included.

## Phases
