|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | [Rate a resolved ticket](phase-01-rate-ticket.md) | 1, 2, 3 | ACT, hot path (tenant scoping) | todo |
| 2 | [Email on a low score](phase-02-low-score-email.md) | 4 | ACT | todo |
| 3 | [Weekly agent summary job](phase-03-weekly-summary.md) | 5 | ACT | todo |
| 4 | [Rename assignee_id to owner_id](phase-04-rename-owner.md) | 6 | **COUNCIL** (export contract, production column) | todo, blocked on Q1/Q7 answers |
| 5 | [Review, docs, handoff](phase-05-review-docs-handoff.md) | all | ACT | todo |

Dependencies: 2 needs 1; 3 needs 1; 4 needs 1-3 merged (it renames their code); 5 last.

## Files
Create: `test/rating.test.js`, `src/jobs/agent-csat-summary.js`, `test/agent-csat-summary.test.js`.
Modify: `src/tickets.js`, `src/portal.js`, `src/jobs/export-tickets.js` (phase 4), `test/tickets.test.js`, `test/export-tickets.test.js`, `docs/glossary.md`, `README.md`.

## Validation questions (answered by recommendation; the owner confirms or changes)
- **Q1. The rename breaks the finance reporting job** (it reads `assignee_id` from `exports/tickets.json` and deploys on its own schedule). *Answer:* the export writes both `owner_id` and `assignee_id` (same value) until finance confirms they read `owner_id`; then the alias is removed in a later change. Everything else is renamed. This is the one place the spec's "everywhere" is not met; the acceptance line stays true for the store, code, tests and docs.
- **Q2. Can a closed ticket be rated?** *Answer:* no. The glossary says a closed ticket is never changed again, and the spec only allows resolved. A customer has about three days (`QUIET_DAYS`, `src/jobs/close-resolved.js:5`) before auto-close; they can reply to reopen if they want more time.
- **Q3. Low score on an unassigned ticket.** `notifyAgent` throws without an agent (`src/notify.js:7`). *Answer:* the rating is stored, no email is queued, no error.
- **Q4. Where does the weekly summary go?** The spec says "writes" without a place. *Answer:* `exports/agent-csat-weekly.json`, an array of `{agent_id, ratings, average}`, average rounded to two decimals, agents with no ratings in the window omitted. Not added to `tickets.json` (finance's contract).
- **Q5. Which agent gets a rating?** *Answer:* the ticket's current assignee when the job runs (`owner_id` after phase 4); a ticket with no assignee is not counted. The window is the rating time (`rated_at`), seven days back, inclusive of exactly seven days.
- **Q6. Rating then reopen.** A customer rates, then replies and reopens, and the ticket is resolved again. *Answer:* the rating stays and no second rating is allowed ("at most one", requirement 2).
- **Q7. Production schema.** The Postgres store is not in this repo. Phase 1 adds two columns (`rating_score`, `rated_at`) and phase 4 renames one. *Answer:* the migrations are written and reviewed outside this plan (COUNCIL), applied before the matching code ships; this plan changes the in-memory store only and lists the exact column changes in the handoff. The duplicate-rating guard must also be enforced in Postgres (`UPDATE ... WHERE rating_score IS NULL`), since the in-memory check-then-write is not atomic across two requests.
- **Q8. Rename timing.** *Answer:* phases 1-3 ship first; phase 4 ships only after Q1 (finance told) and Q7 (column migration ready). Phase 4 is a separate commit/PR so it can be held or reverted alone.

